{
	title: 'Terminal chrome: prompt box between rules, a help row that never jumps',
	spec: "Below the transcript the terminal draws, top to bottom, as the old Hal did (artifact tasks/5p/old-render-status.ts: renderPrompt, ruleText, renderHelpBar; tasks/p0/old-help-bar.ts): the tab bar row; the prompt box between two full-width rules in the input colour, the top rule carrying the fold count (↑N rows scrolled above) at its left and the session's activity word centred (processing, thinking, writing, running <tool>, retrying in …, paused, error, blocked: log in, waiting for answer; from states.describe, task ae). The activity is a word or two, never a message: a clipped login error there is a bug. The whole sentence for a stopped session (the login error, why it retries) is the notice row above the tab bar (app.why); a pause shows no notice, since the transcript's [paused] line and the help row's enter: continue say it (only a pause reason, such as the round cap, is shown), the bottom rule ↓N; the status row (task that follows); then one help row. The help row is always exactly one row, so the prompt never jumps (the user: removing a '/' made the completion row vanish and the prompt jump a row). It shows, in priority order: the hint for an open question (the keys forms really take, tasks/w4/forms.md: e.g. ←/→: choose, a first letter answers, enter: submit, esc: pause), the edit hint while editing the last prompt, completion choices while there are any (clipped to one row), else the key hints for the state (idle with text: enter: send, shift-enter: newline, alt-enter: queue; working: esc: pause; working with text: enter: steer, alt-enter: queue, shift-enter: newline, esc: pause; paused or failed: enter: continue / retry), with '/keys: shortcuts' right-aligned. Hints are key colour + description colour as in the old Hal. The chrome's height depends only on the prompt's rows. Tests: chrome height is the same with and without completion choices, with a question, and while working; each state's hints; the activity word in the top rule.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Shape: client/help-row.ts is the help row (helpRow.row(view, cols), pure; question > editing > choices > state keys). frame.build draws the chrome as: blank row, tab bar, top rule (promptView.rule(cols, '↑N', view.activity) in colors.input(), full terminal width, no PAD), prompt rows, bottom rule ('↓N'), then the help row last. The spot for task 1g's status row is marked in frame.build between the bottom rule and helpRow.row.",
		"This supersedes 8m's dim 'up N'/'down N' rules that appeared only when rows were hidden: both rules are always drawn now, so promptView.box returns the hidden counts (above, below) as numbers, not rule strings.",
		"View gained activity (top rule) and editing (amend.hint, shown in the help row). app.activity(t) maps state to the word: blocked on a question 'waiting for answer', paused 'paused' (or 'paused: reason'), error 'error: <message>' (the state event can come without a turn-end item, so the message must show somewhere), else states.describe(state, Date.now(), items). The notice block above the prompt now holds only passing notices (rejections, warnings), no longer the state description or the edit hint.",
		"Question hints follow hal2's real form keys (common/forms.ts step), not the old Hal's wording: '←/→: choose, first letter: answer' for a choice with several options, 'tab: next field' with several fields, then 'enter: submit, esc: pause' (Escape pauses the session in hal2; it does not abort). form-view's own dim hint row inside the question is still there and now repeats the help row.",
		"'/keys: shortcuts' shows only with the state key hints (as in the old Hal); question, edit and completion rows use the whole width. Blank prompt text (spaces, newlines) counts as no text.",
